{
  "id": "agentstack-labs/linear",
  "version": "0.2.8",
  "name": "Linear Project Management",
  "description": "Batch-triage your Linear backlog behind a human approval gate.\n\nMonday triage is death by a thousand clicks: thirty issues arrived over the weekend, each needing an owner, a priority and a state. The UI is thirty round trips; a script is fast but unreviewable — nobody sees what is about to change, and nothing records who approved it. This module stages the whole batch as one command: RailCall previews it, a human approves once, and the run leaves a receipt whose approval hash is bound to that exact payload.\n\nWHO IT IS FOR: small engineering teams running triage, sprints and releases in Linear who need an audit trail when someone asks who closed those twelve tickets.\n\n45 COMMANDS. Issues (10): list, get, create, update, delete, archive, unarchive, search, bulk_update, link. Search uses Linear's own engine, so descriptions and comments match — not just titles. Archive is the reversible counterpart to delete. Teams (2), Projects (3), Users (2), Workflow states (3), Labels (3), Cycles (4), Comments (4), Webhooks (4) with explicit scoping, Project milestones (3). Initiatives (6) — Linear's roadmap: create, update, roll projects up under a goal, and post health updates (onTrack/atRisk/offTrack).\n\nCOMPOSES AS A WORKFLOW: search_issues to select, bulk_update_issues to act, create_comment for an audit note, link_issues for blockers. If Linear rate-limits mid-batch the command stops and returns not_attempted, so a re-run resumes where it left off.\n\nAIRLOCK GATING: 18 reads run immediately. All 27 writes are write_requires_approval — each previews, waits for a human, emits a receipt. Deletes are high risk. Mutations are never auto-retried: Linear has no idempotency key, so a retry after an accepted write would duplicate it.\n\nSETUP (two minutes): run `railcall studio`, open Sends, pick 'Linear — API key + team' and save your key plus team UUID. That team becomes the default for every team-scoped command, so calls never repeat the UUID.\n\nSECURITY: the key lives in the station vault; the published bundle reads no environment variable at all — the build strips both the standalone credential fallback and the Redis cache config, so the shipped file has zero os.environ reads. Never persisted, never written into a cache key or receipt. Receipts store field names and a hash, not values. GraphQL arguments travel as typed variables. Stdlib urllib only — zero dependencies.\n\nVerified against a live Linear workspace: all 45 commands exercised end-to-end across 56 live tests, plus 240 unit tests. MIT. https://github.com/faizalmy/railcall-linear-module\n\ncontest:2026Q3",
  "author": "AgentStack Labs — RailCall modules for engineering workflow tooling",
  "license": "MIT",
  "publisher_pubkey": "a02b37627cdf4e585c6e72e8335ff299c9d8a3e0720281c76efbb9d06fac3959",
  "category": "Eng",
  "tags": [
    "project-management",
    "issue-tracker",
    "linear",
    "productivity",
    "team-collaboration"
  ],
